---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Practical limits and safety information for Driveway Mechanic automotive guides."
  noIndex={true}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">Disclaimer</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-red-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-red-500/10 to-transparent p-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-red-600 text-white shrink-0">
            <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-700 dark:text-red-400 mb-2">Before working on a vehicle</h2>
            <p class="text-red-600 dark:text-red-300">
              Repair work can cause serious injury or damage. Use instructions for your exact vehicle, follow the manufacturer's precautions, and stop if the procedure or work conditions are unclear.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What these guides can and cannot do</h2>
      <p>
        The site provides general automotive information. A guide cannot inspect your vehicle, confirm its configuration, or diagnose the cause of a symptom. Procedures and specifications can vary by model year, engine, trim, and installed equipment. Check the owner's manual and current manufacturer service information for the exact vehicle before starting work.
      </p>

      <h2>Safety and when to stop</h2>
      <p>
        Vehicle work can involve heavy parts, hot or pressurized fluids, hazardous materials, electrical systems, and tools that can cause injury. Follow the service procedure and equipment instructions for the job. Never rely on a jack alone to support a vehicle while working underneath it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stop and get help from a qualified technician if the vehicle is unstable, the required equipment is unavailable, a safety-critical step is unclear, or the work involves systems you are not equipped to service, such as brakes, steering, airbags, fuel, or high-voltage components.
      </p>

      <h2>Vehicle and product fit</h2>
      <p>
        A part, tool, specification, or procedure mentioned in a guide may not fit every vehicle or situation. Confirm the exact part number, vehicle application, and manufacturer requirements before buying or installing anything. Product details and availability can change; check the manufacturer's current information.
      </p>

      <h2>External product links</h2>
      <p>
        Product links are provided as references. A link does not establish that a product is right for your vehicle or that the site has tested it. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure" class="text-accent hover:underline">affiliate disclosure</a> for the current statement about paid product relationships.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg font-semibold mt-8">
        If you are unsure whether a repair is safe for you to perform, pause and consult a qualified automotive technician.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/60 mt-8">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 22, 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
